# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# SUPABASE CONFIGURATION:
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL: Your Supabase Project URL (e.g. https://your-project.supabase.co)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=""

# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Your Supabase Public Anon Key
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""

# VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_LOGIN: Opt-in, disabled by default. When unset (or any
# value other than the literal string "true"), the "Demo Accounts"
# no-password instant sign-in option is hidden entirely. Only set this to
# "true" in a local .env.local for development — never on a public
# deployment (Vercel, etc.), since it lets anyone with the URL sign in as
# any role with no password.
VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_LOGIN="false"

# Temporary REAL employee account setup UI. Production builds require "true".
# The Edge Function also requires its own server-only opt-in and origin setting.
# This flag does not grant access: Auth + the real public.users role are checked.
VITE_ENABLE_EMPLOYEE_TESTING_MODE="false"

# Server-only secrets for supabase/functions/employee-test-account, set on the
# Edge Function deployment (not VITE_ variables):
# EMPLOYEE_TEST_ACCOUNT_SETUP_ENABLED="true"
# EMPLOYEE_TEST_ALLOWED_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"
# EMPLOYEE_TEST_PROTECTED_TOQA_AUTH_ID / EMPLOYEE_TEST_PROTECTED_SHAHD_AUTH_ID: the two Auth IDs
# that can never have their password reset via that function — also read by
# employee-impersonation below (same protection, one shared pair of secrets).

# TEMPORARY TRANSITION FEATURE — intended for removal once every employee has adopted their own
# real, self-set password. Lets Head of Technical / AI Engineer log into a rank-and-file
# employee's account via a one-time Supabase Auth magic link, without ever seeing or resetting
# that employee's real password. See supabase/functions/employee-impersonation/index.ts and
# src/components/EmployeeImpersonation.tsx.
VITE_ENABLE_EMPLOYEE_IMPERSONATION="false"

# Server-only secrets for supabase/functions/employee-impersonation, set on the Edge Function
# deployment (not VITE_ variables). Independent on/off switch from
# EMPLOYEE_TEST_ACCOUNT_SETUP_ENABLED above, so this can be toggled without affecting Testing
# Mode, and removed outright later without touching that function at all:
# EMPLOYEE_IMPERSONATION_ENABLED="true"
# EMPLOYEE_IMPERSONATION_ALLOWED_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"

# In-app replacement for manually running scripts/provisionAuthUsers.ts /
# scripts/resendRecoveryLink.ts — an authorized admin (canAddEmployees's role set) can
# send/resend a real password-setup link from EmployeeAdminHub.tsx directly. No VITE_ flag: unlike
# Testing Mode/Impersonation above, this is a permanent part of onboarding, not a temporary bridge
# feature, so the button is gated only by role (canAddEmployees), same as "Add Employee" itself.
# Server-only secrets for supabase/functions/employee-invitation, set on the Edge Function
# deployment (not VITE_ variables):
# EMPLOYEE_INVITATION_ENABLED="true"
# EMPLOYEE_INVITATION_ALLOWED_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"

# The two variables below are for scripts/provisionAuthUsers.ts and scripts/resendRecoveryLink.ts
# — the manually-run terminal fallback for the employee-invitation Edge Function above, not the
# app itself. Kept for when the in-app action can't be used (e.g. no deployed Edge Function yet,
# or a bulk one-off sweep). Do not add a
# VITE_ prefix to either: Vite inlines anything prefixed VITE_ into the
# browser bundle, and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY must never reach the
# browser. See the script's own header comment and the chat message that
# introduced it for exactly how to set these for a single run without
# writing the key to disk at all.
# SUPABASE_URL: same value as VITE_SUPABASE_URL above (not secret).
SUPABASE_URL=""
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> service_role, in the Supabase dashboard. SECRET — bypasses RLS entirely.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""

# AI Orchestrator (supabase/functions/ai-router) — Phase 1 of 6: provider adapters + Edge Function
# skeleton only, no Task Registry/rotation/usage-tracking yet. No VITE_ flag: unlike Testing
# Mode/Impersonation, this isn't a bridge tool with its own UI to gate — each of the 4 features it
# will power (Phase 5) is already gated by its own existing permission check, same as "Generate
# Report"/"Add Employee" today.
# Providers: Gemini (extraction stage) + Groq (analysis stage, primary) + OpenRouter free models
# (analysis stage, emergency fallback only — its free tier is roughly 50 requests/day unless the
# account has purchased $10+ of credits). Grok/xAI was evaluated and dropped: it has no renewing
# free tier (a one-time $25 signup credit, then real paid charges), which doesn't fit this
# project's zero-AI-cost goal. ONE key per provider only — never multiple accounts/keys to pool
# free quotas (both providers' ToS forbid it); if a single account's quota proves insufficient in
# practice, the fix is a paid tier upgrade on that same account, not another account.
# Server-only secrets, set on the Edge Function deployment (not VITE_ variables):
# AI_ROUTER_ENABLED="true"
# AI_ROUTER_ALLOWED_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"
# GEMINI_API_KEY: from Google AI Studio. This was previously declared at the top of this file as
# an AI-Studio-scaffold leftover (and even mistakenly typed into src/vite-env.d.ts's client-side
# ImportMetaEnv, though never actually consumed there) — this Edge Function is its first real,
# server-only consumer. Optional GEMINI_MODEL override (default: gemini-2.5-flash) since free-tier
# model names/quotas have already changed twice in 2026.
# GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"
# GEMINI_MODEL="gemini-2.5-flash"
# GROQ_API_KEY: from console.groq.com. GROQ_MODEL is REQUIRED, no default — this sandbox's network
# egress proxy blocked a direct read of console.groq.com/docs/models while building this, and
# secondary sources disagreed on which models are currently free (some still list Llama 3.1/3.3,
# which other sources say were removed from Groq's free tier in August 2026). Check the live model
# list yourself and set the exact current free model id before deploying.
# GROQ_API_KEY="MY_GROQ_API_KEY"
# GROQ_MODEL=""
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY: from openrouter.ai/keys. OPENROUTER_MODEL is REQUIRED, no default, same
# reasoning as GROQ_MODEL above — OpenRouter's free (":free"-suffixed) model roster rotates over
# time; set it to a currently free model id from openrouter.ai/models before deploying.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY="MY_OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=""

